FoldJAX vendors the Apache-2.0 OpenFold3 data definitions and NumPy preprocessing
helpers required for standalone inference under `_upstream/`. Training, model,
and tensor-runtime modules are not included. Compatibility changes are limited
to the FoldJAX package namespace, NumPy-only MSA parsing, and local data loading.

The vendored files were refreshed from the OpenFold3 v0.5.0 tag (commit
c4771653, 2026-09-30). Apart from the package namespace, they differ from
that commit only as follows:
- openfold3/__init__.py lists only the vendored subpackages and drops the
  DeepSpeed import hook.
- core/data/io/sequence/msa.py reads pre-parsed .npz alignments from plain
  <database>__msa / __deletion_matrix / __metadata arrays with
  allow_pickle=False, instead of pickled object arrays.
- core/data/io/structure/cif.py drops parse_RNA_monomer_cif_tmp, a training
  helper that reads through the unvendored boto3-backed io.s3.
- core/data/io/structure/mol.py inlines is_intlike_string from the unvendored
  io.utils.
- core/data/primitives/structure/template.py imports get_token_starts from
  primitives.structure.labels; the torch-importing featurization.structure
  only re-exports it.
- core/data/tools/kalign.py bounds the kalign LRU cache to 32 entries.
core/config/pocket_sampling_config.py is vendored so the query schema parses
pocket_constraint; FoldJAX refuses queries that set it.

core/data/resources/patches.py contains three functions that upstream copied
from Biotite (https://github.com/biotite-dev/biotite), Copyright 2017, The
Biotite contributors, under the BSD 3-Clause License. That licence is
reproduced in FoldJAX's THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES (repository root; in a wheel,
the foldjax-*.dist-info/licenses/ directory).
